ignment options for virtual reality properties \n- Multi-Object Labels \u2013 Labels can now target multiple objects simultaneously  \n- Partial Language Support \u2013 Ability to download lessons in partially supported languages  \n- Performance Enhancements \u2013 lesson flow view and hit point rendering speed  ", "created_date": 1789046053, "id": "28627842590234608", "version": "2.2.4", "version_code": 202041342, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "5157340111044853", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "28627842590234608"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "744280593379280"}]}, "change_log": "Version 2.2.3 - Player\n- Enhanced Mesh Importer: We\u2019ve expanded our file compatibility. The improved importer now supports a wider range of 3D mesh formats, reducing the need for external pre-processing and allowing for more diverse asset integration.\n- Spatial 3D Audio: Elevate realism with distance-based sound. You can now create audio objects that dynamically attenuate (fade) as the user moves away from the source, providing a natural sense of scale and presence.\n- Multi-Script State Support: You can now attach and run multiple scripts within a single state. This allows for cleaner organization of complex behaviors and more modular logic design.", "created_date": 1778074020, "id": "26945655385120012", "version": "2.2.3", "version_code": 202031400, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "Andr